course: dictionary
lesson: 20
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things. Abs is one of them. The word alone is not enough, so read the words around it to find which meaning is meant. This is context at work, just as in the last lesson.
explain: «Lee's abs ached after PE» is about the body. Abs here are muscles, short for abdominal muscles, the ones at the front of your tummy. A «six-pack» shows these muscles, and people «work their abs» to make them stronger.
explain: «ABS anti-lock brakes» is about cars. ABS in capitals is a safety system, not muscles. Its letters stand for anti-lock braking system, which stops a car's wheels locking when the driver brakes hard.
explain: ABS is also a hard plastic used for things like LEGO bricks. Ask yourself: is the sentence about the body, a car, or a material? That question tells you which meaning you need.
fact: Abs is short for abdominal muscles, the stomach muscles.
fact: ABS in capitals stands for anti-lock braking system.
fact: «ABS anti-lock brakes notice when a wheel stops turning and skids», then release and press the brakes many times a second so the driver can still steer.
fact: ABS is also a hard plastic used for things like LEGO bricks.
fact: Context tells you which meaning is right: muscles, a car safety system, or a plastic material.
exercise: «ABS anti-lock brakes notice when a wheel stops turning and skids.» What does ABS mean in this sentence? | A type of sports shoe | *A car safety system | A set of stomach muscles | A hard plastic toy brick
exercise: Ella says her six-pack abs are sore after PE. What are abs? | The wheels of a car | A pair of trainers | A hard plastic | *The muscles at the front of the stomach
exercise: Sam's LEGO brick is made from ABS. What is ABS in this sentence? | A brake system | A kind of football | Stomach muscles | *A hard plastic
test: «ABS stops a car's wheels from locking when the driver brakes hard.» What is ABS here? | Hard plastic for toys | Stomach muscles | *Anti-lock braking system | A gym class
test: Which phrase is about muscles, not cars? | ABS brakes | ABS system | *Six-pack abs | ABS plastic
exam: In «Lee's abs ached after PE», what are abs? | *Stomach muscles | Plastic bricks | Car brakes | A safety system
